# Think wider

Theo refines "bigger" into "wider" and distinguishes the range a product covers from the feature count in one area. [13:07](https://youtu.be/xUnRQ9vLXxo?t=787) [13:23](https://youtu.be/xUnRQ9vLXxo?t=803).

He says an extensible architecture can let users build vertical features the product author did not predict. [14:37](https://youtu.be/xUnRQ9vLXxo?t=877).

See [AI Engineer World's Fair 2026](/lore/aiewf-2026-everything-we-knew-about-software-has-changed-theo-browne) and [Theo Browne](/lore/theo-browne).
